4.TERNARY SEARCH
Given a sorted array of n elements. Write a function to search a given element x in the array using Ternary Search. Return the index of x in the array. If x is not present in the array, return -1.
SOURCE CODE :
        class Solution {
            public boolean ternarySearch(int[] arr, int x) {
                // code here
                int low=0;
                int high=arr.length-1;
                while(low<=high){
                    int mid1=low+(high-low)/3;
                    int mid2=high-(high-low)/3;
                    if(arr[mid1]==x || arr[mid2]==x){
                        return true;
                    }
                    else if(arr[mid1]>x){
                        high=mid1-1;
                    }
                    else if(arr[mid2]<x){
                        low=mid2+1;
                    }
                    else{
                        low=mid1+1;
                        high=mid2-1;
                    }
                }
                return false;
            }
        }
